---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Run one hook for a host's event: read from stdin, answered on stdout in the host's own protocol

Usage: specforge hook [OPTIONS] --host <HOST> --event <EVENT> <ROUTE>

Arguments:
  <ROUTE>
          The hook: the extension's short name, a dot and the hook's id (`gsd.write_guard`)

Options:
      --host <HOST>
          The host that ran it: claude-code, codex or cursor

      --event <EVENT>
          The event the hook is wired to: pre_tool, post_tool, pre_commit, user_prompt, session_start, stop, subagent_start, subagent_stop, pre_compact or statusline

      --tools <TOOLS>
          Tool classes the hook fires on, comma-separated (empty: any tool)

      --paths <PATHS>
          Project-relative globs a path of the tool's input must match, comma-separated (empty: any path)

  -h, --help
          Print help
